  "notes": "Modified cash basis city. Trimmed PDF has 20 pages (63 in original): p1 Statement of Net Position, pp2-4 Statement of Activities, pp5-6 governmental funds balance sheet, pp7-8 revenues, pp9-10 expenditures/changes in fund balances, pp11-12 proprietary Statement of Net Position, pp13-14 proprietary revenues/expenses, pp15-16 proprietary cash flows, pp17-18 total primary government budgetary comparison, pp19-20 schedule of expenditures. Governmental amounts use the Total column. Governmental identity: 572,634 + 673,960 - 608,480 + 170,500 + 35,154 = 843,768. Ending_cash is the fund balance rolled forward (843,768); cash in bank/treasurer is 851,268 with 7,500 due to other funds. Business-type: from the proprietary funds Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Fund Net Position (pp13-14, Totals column; accrual, so measure = net position), added by the v8 re-trim. It replaces the earlier figures derived from the combined budget schedule (one derived receipts line 1,345,483, utility function lines 1,383,409 and a -170,500 contra line, cash 1,065,827 -> 1,027,901), and resolves both earlier decision_needed questions: the 170,500 transfers to governmental funds are printed as proprietary Transfers (Electric 149,000, Water 21,500; p14). Business roll: 2,736,965 + 1,345,265 - 1,180,949 - 170,500 = 2,730,781. Proprietary cash flow statement (pp15-16; cash in bank 1,058,327 -> 1,020,401) and Statement of Net Position (pp11-12: total assets 3,454,025, liabilities 723,244, net position 2,730,781) also trimmed; proprietary field left null as the report is cash basis. Statement of Net Position p1 (total net position 5,712,685; governmental 2,981,904 includes capital assets) prints net position only, so it cannot serve as a combined balance sheet. balance_sheet combines the governmental funds balance sheet Total column (p6; cash-basis, no capital assets) with the proprietary funds Statement of Net Position Totals column (pp11-12), each line tagged with fund_type; totals are the sums of the two printed totals (computed). The 7,500 due to other funds (governmental) and due from other funds (Water) are both kept as printed, not eliminated. Detail: only the governmental Schedule of Expenditures by object (Total column, 8 fund columns exceed 6, so combined); the budget schedule on pp17-18: its receipts and governmental function lines mix funds and duplicate the statements, so they are not recorded; its four business-type lines (Electric, Solid Waste, Sewer, Water; actual and budget, p18) are recorded in detail as not itemized, with a -170,500 contra line and an other financing line for the transfers to governmental funds that the proprietary statement (p14) shows but the budget schedule hides inside those lines. No printed business-type subtotal, so no detail_totals for them. Read pages 1-20 of 20"
}